# Netlify-format redirects. Equivalent 301s are needed at the server level on
# other hosts. Rules are evaluated top to bottom; the first match wins.

# 1. Canonical host — never serve the site on the apex domain as a duplicate.
https://unitedtermitenj.net/* https://www.unitedtermitenj.net/:splat 301!
http://unitedtermitenj.net/*  https://www.unitedtermitenj.net/:splat 301!

# 2. Old Hibu site -> new site.
#    The service page slugs were kept identical on purpose, so those URLs
#    (termite-inspections.html, termite-control.html, pest-control.html,
#    crawl-space-services.html, reviews.html, contact.html) already resolve
#    with no rule needed. Only these old URLs have no direct counterpart:
/index.html            /                301!
/video-splash-pop.html /                301
/referrer.html         /                301

# The old mirror also exposed crawler artifacts (/signals/*, /_dm/*, e.html,
# n.html, o.html, t.html and similar). They were never linked publicly; they
# fall through to 404.html, which is the correct signal for Google.
